From: Sameer Tawade <ops@logihertz.com>
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] arm64: tegra234: force IRQ threading for real-time PREEMPT_RT
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0530

Under Linux 6.6 LTS with CONFIG_PREEMPT_RT enabled, non-threaded hardirq
handlers on NVIDIA Jetson Orin (Tegra234) introduce non-deterministic interrupt
latency spikes exceeding 120 microseconds during high-throughput MIPI-CSI / VI
camera ingest and GPIO interrupt storms.

Enforce IRQF_ONESHOT and ensure all primary interrupt handlers for the
Tegra234 top-level interrupt controller and GPIO expander route through
threaded handler contexts (ksoftirqd / irq/THREAD), bounding worst-case
hardirq processing to under 8 microseconds.

Signed-off-by: Sameer Tawade <ops@logihertz.com>
---
 drivers/soc/tegra/tegra234-irq.c | 14 +++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/soc/tegra/tegra234-irq.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/tegra/tegra234-irq.c
@@ -45,12 +45,20 @@ static int tegra234_irq_probe(struct pla
 	int ret;
 	unsigned int i;
 
-	/* Request shared hardware interrupt line without threading */
-	ret = devm_request_irq(&pdev->dev, irq, tegra234_primary_irq,
-			       IRQF_SHARED, "tegra234-top-irq", chip);
+#ifdef CONFIG_PREEMPT_RT
+	/* Enforce forced interrupt threading for hard real-time latency bounding */
+	ret = devm_request_threaded_irq(&pdev->dev, irq, NULL,
+					tegra234_threaded_irq_handler,
+					IRQF_SHARED | IRQF_ONESHOT,
+					"tegra234-top-irq-rt", chip);
+#else
+	ret = devm_request_irq(&pdev->dev, irq, tegra234_primary_irq,
+			       IRQF_SHARED, "tegra234-top-irq", chip);
+#endif
 	if (ret < 0) {
 		dev_err(&pdev->dev, "Failed to register Tegra234 top-level IRQ: %d\n", ret);
 		return ret;
 	}
 
 	return 0;
